{
  "dom_id": "step-q113337",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of $y=-\\frac{5}{2x}?$",
  "worked_solution": "To plot $y=-\\frac{5}{2x},$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=-\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266548/assets/d5d93e12275c683e0a56f0ec9a0c99540a7774879cd0f8fa69151ddba68a44fa.png)\n\n- Stretch the result by a scale factor of $\\frac{5}{2}$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=-\\frac{5}{2x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266548/assets/3bc730306eaa88729b46b20ddb32782c89186f6db66c51fd924b2622804396aa.png)",
